:Namespace Search
    ⍝ Choice of the move to play.

    ⎕IO ⎕ML←1

    ⍝ Score of a side that is checkmated at the root. It exceeds any
    ⍝ material score, so no material balance outweighs a mate.
    MATE←100000

    negamax←{
        ⍝ Score of a position by negamax search to a fixed depth.
        ⍝ ⍺ ←→ lookup tables
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ depth, bitboards, game state[, ply]; ply defaults to 0
        ⍝ ← ←→ score in centipawns from the side to move's point of view;
        ⍝      a side checkmated ply half-moves from the root scores
        ⍝      ply-MATE, so faster mates score higher for the winner

        lookups←⍺
        (depth bitboards game_state ply)←4↑⍵,0

        side←game_state[##.GameState.side]
        in_check←lookups ##.MoveGeneration.isKingInCheck bitboards side

         ⍝ Check extension: the search continues past the horizon while in
        ⍝ check, so a mate there is still found.
        (depth≤0)∧~in_check:##.Evaluation.evaluate bitboards game_state

        moves←lookups ##.MoveGeneration.generateLegalMoves bitboards game_state
        side←game_state[##.GameState.side]
        ⍝ If there are no legal moves, it is either stalemate (evaluation 0)
        ⍝ or checkmate (evaluation ply-MATE).
        0=≢moves:in_check×ply-MATE

        ⍝ Each child's score is from the opponent's point of view, so it is
        ⍝ negated before taking the maximum.
        ⌈/-lookups{⍺ negamax (depth-1),(bitboards game_state ##.MoveGeneration.makeMove ⍵),ply+1}⍤1⊢moves
    }

    bestMove←{
        ⍝ Move with the highest negamax score.
        ⍝ ⍺ ←→ lookup tables
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ depth, bitboards, game state
        ⍝ ← ←→ move (from to promotion); ⍬ when there is no legal move

        lookups←⍺
        (depth bitboards game_state)←⍵

        moves←lookups ##.MoveGeneration.generateLegalMoves bitboards game_state
        0=≢moves:⍬

        ⍝ The positions after the root moves are one ply from the root.
        scores←-lookups{⍺ negamax(depth-1),(bitboards game_state ##.MoveGeneration.makeMove ⍵),1}⍤1⊢moves

        ⍝ Pick one of the best moves at random to keep variety.
        best←moves⌿⍨scores=⌈/scores
        best[?≢best;] 
    }

    randomMove←{
        ⍝ Uniformly random legal move.
        ⍝ ⍺ ←→ lookup tables
        ⍝ ⍵ ←→ bitboards, game state
        ⍝ ← ←→ move (from to promotion); ⍬ when there is no legal move

        moves←⍺ ##.MoveGeneration.generateLegalMoves ⍵
        0=≢moves:⍬
        moves[?≢moves;]
    }
:EndNamespace